  "executive_briefing": "The 2026 corporate tax landscape is dominated by a clear divergence between US domestic policy and the OECD's Pillar Two framework, catalyzed by the US 'One Big Beautiful Bill Act' (OBBBA) which prioritizes localized incentives like the 14% effective rate on foreign-market income. While the global minimum tax consensus faces fatigue, jurisdictions such as Portugal and Singapore are aggressively engineering tax rates and non-taxable grants to maintain competitiveness. Simultaneously, a significant breakthrough in trade policy has emerged as US courts have ruled certain IEEPA-based tariffs unlawful, creating a judicial check on executive protectionism. On the compliance front, the transition to real-time transactional reporting is accelerating, with Singapore's mandatory InvoiceNow framework (2025-2031) serving as the global benchmark for Peppol-based GST enforcement.",
